# ============================================================================
# TERRAFORM ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES - env.example
# ============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env and edit it for your clusters:
#   cp env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit it.
#
# make reads .env by itself; you do not need to source it. make parses the file,
# so keep each line as KEY=value: no spaces around "=", no quotes.
#
# A value here replaces the Makefile default. `make <command> KEY=value`
# replaces it for that one run only.
#
# Each cluster's commands use that cluster's variables:
#   default workspace    TFVARS_FILE
#   on-prem workspace    TFVARS_ON_PREM       BOOTSTRAP_TFVARS_ON_PREM
#   on-cloud workspace   TFVARS_ON_CLOUD      BOOTSTRAP_TFVARS_ON_CLOUD
# ============================================================================

# --- default workspace: plan / apply / destroy ---
# Makefile default: terraform.tfvars
TFVARS_FILE=terraform.tfvars

# --- on-prem workspace: apply-on-prem / destroy-on-prem (stage 2) ---
# Makefile default: terraform.tfvars.example
TFVARS_ON_PREM=terraform.on-prem.tfvars

# --- on-cloud workspace: apply-on-cloud / destroy-on-cloud (stage 2) ---
# Makefile default: terraform.tfvars.example
TFVARS_ON_CLOUD=terraform.on-cloud.tfvars

# --- stage 1 (bootstrap) ---
# Makefile defaults: the two committed examples below.
BOOTSTRAP_TFVARS_ON_PREM=terraform.bootstrap.on-prem.tfvars.example
BOOTSTRAP_TFVARS_ON_CLOUD=terraform.bootstrap.on-cloud.tfvars.example

# --- Terraform parallelism for the apply targets ---
# Reduce for MicroK8s/SQLite to prevent database locks; raise for cloud API limits.
# Remove the line to auto-detect (2 on MicroK8s, 10 otherwise).
TFVARS_PARALLELISM=2

# ============================================================================
# Usage
# ============================================================================
#   make bootstrap-on-prem     # Stage 1: minimal core only
#   make apply-on-prem         # Stage 2: full apply (gated on working storage)
#   make bootstrap-on-cloud
#   make apply-on-cloud
#   Add -auto- to skip confirmation: make bootstrap-auto-on-prem
#
# To see which var-file a command will use, without running it:
#   make -n apply-on-prem
# ============================================================================
